  "meta": {
    "document": "Bastrop County FY2025-26 Adopted Budget",
    "title": "Bastrop County — the money trail",
    "grand_total": 93738915,
    "year": 2026,
    "note": "Texas counties budget fund by fund, not as one grand total. This is the tax-supported budget — the General Fund (most offices and courts), the Road & Bridge Fund, and Debt Service — adopted by the Commissioners Court on August 25, 2025 for the fiscal year beginning October 1, 2025. It is paid for mostly by property tax: the adopted rate is $0.42870 per $100 of value (General Fund $0.350500 + Road & Bridge $0.078210), levied on $13,474,499,007 of certified taxable value. The county adopted at its voter-approval rate — the most it could set without an election. Capital-project and grant funds are budgeted separately and left out here because they double-count transfers; every figure below traces to the county's adopted budget."
  },
